$\vec F=\frac{d \vec p}{dt}$

for constant mass:

$\vec F=m \vec a$

$W= \Delta E$

for constant force $F$ along a path $s$ (force and displacement parallel)

$W=F \cdot s$

$\eta= \frac{W_\text{useful}}{Q_\text{in}}<1$

$\eta$ indicates what share of supplied heat $Q_\text{in}$ becomes useful work $W_\text{useful}$;
$\eta<1$ because waste heat always remains.
